            <ArticleTitle>Prognostic value of simultaneous perfusion and function assessment using technetium-99m sestamibi.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>562-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study examines the prognostic value of simultaneous perfusion and function assessment in 412 patients. The exercise perfusion pattern was a stronger predictor of events (mostly acute nonfatal myocardial infarcts) than resting ejection fraction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
